# The release gate byte-compares each committed .js with a fresh esbuild of its
# .jsx, and esbuild writes LF. Keep source and build output LF on every clone
# (core.autocrlf=true on Windows would otherwise check them out as CRLF and
# fail the comparison with nothing actually changed).
*.js   text eol=lf
*.jsx  text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

# FE final: the dist-output planted-defect checks edit dist/_headers and
# dist/index.html by exact LF-joined strings, and build-dist.mjs splices the
# app-scripts block on "\n". With core.autocrlf=true a fresh Windows clone
# checked these out as CRLF and the gate failed two canaries with nothing
# changed. Every text file the build copies into dist/ stays LF.
_headers        text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.webmanifest   text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.svg           text eol=lf
